Patch summary:
Keep the Cuttlefish displays added at runtime (Ika's app windows) from being
composed and posted again when nothing on them changed.

- Report every display after the first as EXTERNAL. As INTERNAL displays they
  could host desktops, so WM Shell opened apps there in a desk, with a window
  frame (box shadow and border) that forced client composition of the whole
  display. External displays without system decorations are not desktop
  capable: apps open fullscreen and are composed on the host.
- SurfaceFlinger presents every display whenever one of them changes. With
  host composition, skip a display's present when its layers, their buffers
  and the client target are the same as at its last present and no layer
  reports surface damage (one empty damage rect means unchanged), so that the
  host does not compose, post and stream the same picture again.

--- a/hals/hwc3/Display.cpp
+++ b/hals/hwc3/Display.cpp
